[5.353699, "o", "\r\n"]
[8.352879, "o", "transport corp (http 127.0.0.1:3128)\r\n  reachable         yes\r\n  known-open        open      status 200         0.8ms\r\n  known-closed      error     status 503         0.5ms   <- expected closed\r\n  blackholed        error     status 503      2992.7ms   <- expected filtered\r\n\r\n  fidelity          open_only\r\n  This HTTP CONNECT proxy answered a known-closed destination with status\r\n  503. HTTP standardises no status meaning refused, so scanr records\r\n  non-open results through it as `error` with source `proxy_reply` rather\r\n  than guessing `closed` or `filtered`.\r\n"]
[10.855365, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2;36m# So every non-open port is error, honestly, with the status line in the record.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[11.256772, "o", "\u001b[2;36m# The open set is exact.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
